From 0ba9dda6d096a8929dd373d6f245f61c90e03760 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 18:09:44 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 08/60] TP RoCE: with no TF_TP_ROCE_HCA, each rank picks the
 ports on an IPv4 /24 the peer also has

The automatic pick took the first N active RoCE ports in device-list order and never checked that the peer can reach
them. On a host with two neighbours, one picked port can sit on a subnet the peer does not have, and the queue pair's
RTR step then fails, which reports RoCE unavailable.

Every rank now sends its usable ports' IPv4 addresses over the bootstrap. Each rank then keeps the ports whose /24 the
peer also lists, ordered by subnet and each /24 no more often than both sides have it, so both ranks pick the same
number. With no shared /24 the old first-N order is kept, with a warning to set TF_TP_ROCE_HCA. The exchange runs on
every rank, including ranks that set TF_TP_ROCE_HCA, so the bootstrap stays in step.

(cherry picked from commit 06c4e75f97a7aee994f71abe2074d219ec65cff2)
